{"id":"mahabharata-7-056","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":56,"title":"षट्पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 56 · Krishna prepares for the morrow","summary":{"en":"Krishna enters Arjuna's house, purifies himself, and spreads kusha grass for rites of protection for the next day. He tells his charioteer Daruka that he will so act that Arjuna kills Jayadratha, and bids him prepare his chariot at dawn.","kn":"ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಮನೆ ಪ್ರವೇಶಿಸಿ ಶುದ್ಧನಾಗಿ ಮರುದಿನದ ರಕ್ಷಣಾ ಕರ್ಮಗಳಿಗೆ ದರ್ಭೆ ಹಾಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಜಯದ್ರಥನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುವಂತೆ ತಾನು ಮಾಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಸಾರಥಿ ದಾರುಕನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳಿ ಬೆಳಗ್ಗೆ ರಥ ಸಿದ್ಧಪಡಿಸಲು ಆದೇಶಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण अर्जुन के भवन में प्रवेश कर शुद्ध होते हैं और अगले दिन की रक्षा-विधि के लिए कुश बिछाते हैं। वे सारथी दारुक से कहते हैं कि वे ऐसा करेंगे कि अर्जुन जयद्रथ को मारे, और भोर में रथ तैयार रखने का आदेश देते हैं।","te":"కృష్ణుడు అర్జునుని గృహంలోకి ప్రవేశించి శుద్ధి చేసుకుని మరుసటి రోజు రక్షా కర్మలకు దర్భలు పరుస్తాడు. అర్జునుడు జయద్రథుని చంపేలా తాను చేస్తానని సారథి దారుకునికి చెప్పి ఉదయం రథం సిద్ధం చేయమంటాడు.","ta":"கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனின் மாளிகையில் புகுந்து தூய்மை செய்து மறுநாளின் காப்புச் சடங்குக்குத் தர்ப்பை விரிக்கிறார். அர்ஜுனன் ஜயத்ரதனைக் கொல்லும்படி தாம் செய்வேன் என்று தேரோட்டி தாருகனிடம் கூறி, விடியலில் தேரைத் தயாராக்க ஆணையிடுகிறார்.","ml":"കൃഷ്ണൻ അർജുനന്റെ വീട്ടിൽ പ്രവേശിച്ച് ശുദ്ധിവരുത്തി, പിറ്റേന്നത്തെ രക്ഷാകർമങ്ങൾക്കായി കുശപ്പുല്ല് വിരിക്കുന്നു. ജയദ്രഥനെ അർജുനൻ വധിക്കുന്ന വിധത്തിൽ താൻ പ്രവർത്തിക്കുമെന്ന് സാരഥി ദാരുകനോട് പറയുന്ന അദ്ദേഹം, പുലർച്ചെ തേര് ഒരുക്കാൻ കൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.56; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"प्रतिज्ञापर्व","titleEn":"Pratijna Parva (Arjuna's vow)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनस्य भवनं प्रविश्याप्रतिमं विभुः ।\nस्पृष्ट्वाम्भः पुण्डरीकाक्षः स्थण्डिले शुभलक्षणे ।\nसंतस्तार शुभां शय्यां दर्भैर्वैडूर्यसंनिभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the lord, lotus-eyed Krishna, entered Arjuna's incomparable dwelling, touched water, and on an auspicious level spot spread a lovely bed of darbha grass shining like beryl."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो माल्येन विधिवल्लाजैर्गन्धैः सुमङ्गलैः ।\nअलंचकार तां शय्यां परिवार्यायुधोत्तमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He then adorned that bed according to rule with garlands, parched grain and fragrant, auspicious substances, and set the finest weapons around it."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः स्पृष्टोदकं पार्थं विनीताः परिचारकाः ।\nदर्शयां नैत्यकं चक्रुर्नैशं त्रैयम्बकं बलिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after Partha had touched water, well-trained attendants brought forward the regular night offering to Tryambaka."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततः प्रीतमनाः पार्थो गन्धैर्माल्यैश्च माधवम् ।\nअलंकृत्योपहारं तं नैशमस्मै न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha, pleased, adorned Madhava with perfumes and garlands and presented to him that night offering."}},{"n":5,"text":"स्मयमानस्तु गोविन्दः फल्गुनं प्रत्यभाषत ।\nसुप्यतां पार्थ भद्रं ते कल्याणाय व्रजाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Smiling, Govinda said to Phalguna, \"Sleep, Partha. May you be well. I go for your good.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"स्थापयित्वा ततो द्वाःस्थान्गोप्तॄंश्चात्तायुधान्नरान् ।\nदारुकानुगतः श्रीमान्विवेश शिबिरं स्वकम् ।\nशिश्ये च शयने शुभ्रे बहुकृत्यं विचिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Posting doorkeepers and armed guards, the glorious one, followed by Daruka, entered his own tent and lay on a white bed, thinking of the many tasks ahead."}},{"n":7,"text":"न पाण्डवानां शिबिरे कश्चित्सुष्वाप तां निशाम् ।\nप्रजागरः सर्वजनमाविवेश विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the Pandavas' camp no one slept that night, O lord of men. Wakefulness took hold of every person."}},{"n":8,"text":"पुत्रशोकाभिभूतेन प्रतिज्ञातो महात्मना ।\nसहसा सिन्धुराजस्य वधो गाण्डीवधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"They thought, \"The great-souled wielder of Gandiva, overcome with grief for his son, suddenly vowed the killing of the Sindhu king.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तत्कथं नु महाबाहुर्वासविः परवीरहा ।\nप्रतिज्ञां सफलां कुर्यादिति ते समचिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How will the mighty-armed son of Indra, slayer of enemy heroes, make his vow fruitful?\""}},{"n":10,"text":"कष्टं हीदं व्यवसितं पाण्डवेन महात्मना ।\nपुत्रशोकाभितप्तेन प्रतिज्ञा महती कृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is a hard resolve the great-souled Pandava has made. Burning with grief for his son, he has taken a great vow.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"भ्रातरश्चापि विक्रान्ता बहुलानि बलानि च ।\nधृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्रेण सर्वं तस्मै निवेदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dhritarashtra's son has been told everything, about his brothers' courage and his many forces.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"स हत्वा सैन्धवं संख्ये पुनरेतु धनंजयः ।\nजित्वा रिपुगणांश्चैव पारयत्वर्जुनो व्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"May Dhananjaya kill Saindhava in the battle and return. May Arjuna conquer the hosts of his enemies and fulfil his vow.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"अहत्वा सिन्धुराजं हि धूमकेतुं प्रवेक्ष्यति ।\nन ह्येतदनृतं कर्तुमर्हः पार्थो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If he does not kill the Sindhu king, he will enter the fire. Partha Dhananjaya cannot make this false.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"धर्मपुत्रः कथं राजा भविष्यति मृतेऽर्जुने ।\nतस्मिन्हि विजयः कृत्स्नः पाण्डवेन समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How will King Dharmaputra rule if Arjuna dies? For the whole victory has been entrusted to that Pandava.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"यदि नः सुकृतं किंचिद्यदि दत्तं हुतं यदि ।\nफलेन तस्य सर्वस्य सव्यसाची जयत्वरीन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If we have any merit, if anything has been given or offered in sacrifice, by the fruit of all that may Savyasachin conquer his enemies.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"एवं कथयतां तेषां जयमाशंसतां प्रभो ।\nकृच्छ्रेण महता राजन्रजनी व्यत्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they spoke so, hoping for victory, O king, the night passed with great difficulty."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्यां रजन्यां मध्ये तु प्रतिबुद्धो जनार्दनः ।\nस्मृत्वा प्रतिज्ञां पार्थस्य दारुकं प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the middle of that night Janardana woke, remembered Partha's vow, and said to Daruka."}},{"n":18,"text":"अर्जुनेन प्रतिज्ञातमार्तेन हतबन्धुना ।\nजयद्रथं हनिष्यामि श्वोभूत इति दारुक ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Daruka, Arjuna, in his grief and having lost his kinsman, has vowed, 'Tomorrow I shall kill Jayadratha.'\""}},{"n":19,"text":"तत्तु दुर्योधनः श्रुत्वा मन्त्रिभिर्मन्त्रयिष्यति ।\nयथा जयद्रथं पार्थो न हन्यादिति संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duryodhana, hearing this, will plan with his counsellors how Partha may not kill Jayadratha in battle.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"अक्षौहिण्यो हि ताः सर्वा रक्षिष्यन्ति जयद्रथम् ।\nद्रोणश्च सह पुत्रेण सर्वास्त्रविधिपारगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All those akshauhinis will protect Jayadratha, and so will Drona with his son, who has mastered all weapons.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"एको वीरः सहस्राक्षो दैत्यदानवमर्दिता ।\nसोऽपि तं नोत्सहेताजौ हन्तुं द्रोणेन रक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even Indra of the thousand eyes, the one hero who crushed the Daityas and Danavas, would not dare to kill him in battle when Drona protects him.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"सोऽहं श्वस्तत्करिष्यामि यथा कुन्तीसुतोऽर्जुनः ।\nअप्राप्तेऽस्तं दिनकरे हनिष्यति जयद्रथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So tomorrow I shall do such a thing that Arjuna, son of Kunti, will kill Jayadratha before the sun reaches the setting.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"न हि दारा न मित्राणि ज्ञातयो न च बान्धवाः ।\nकश्चिन्नान्यः प्रियतरः कुन्तीपुत्रान्ममार्जुनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Daruka, there is no wife, friend, relative or kinsman dearer to me than Arjuna, son of Kunti.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"अनर्जुनमिमं लोकं मुहूर्तमपि दारुक ।\nउदीक्षितुं न शक्तोऽहं भविता न च तत्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I could not bear to look on this world without Arjuna even for a moment, and that will not happen.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"अहं ध्वजिन्यः शत्रूणां सहयाः सरथद्विपाः ।\nअर्जुनार्थे हनिष्यामि सकर्णाः ससुयोधनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For Arjuna's sake I shall destroy the enemy armies with their horses, chariots and elephants, with Karna and Suyodhana.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"श्वो निरीक्षन्तु मे वीर्यं त्रयो लोका महाहवे ।\nधनंजयार्थं समरे पराक्रान्तस्य दारुक ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tomorrow let the three worlds see my might in the great battle, when I exert myself for Dhananjaya.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"श्वो नरेन्द्रसहस्राणि राजपुत्रशतानि च ।\nसाश्वद्विपरथान्याजौ विद्रविष्यन्ति दारुक ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tomorrow, Daruka, thousands of kings and hundreds of princes with their horses, elephants and chariots will flee in battle.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"श्वस्तां चक्रप्रमथितां द्रक्ष्यसे नृपवाहिनीम् ।\nमया क्रुद्धेन समरे पाण्डवार्थे निपातिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tomorrow you will see that royal army crushed by my discus, struck down in battle by my anger for the Pandavas' sake.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"श्वः सदेवाः सगन्धर्वाः पिशाचोरगराक्षसाः ।\nज्ञास्यन्ति लोकाः सर्वे मां सुहृदं सव्यसाचिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tomorrow the gods, Gandharvas, pishachas, serpents and rakshasas, all the worlds, will know me as the friend of Savyasachin.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"यस्तं द्वेष्टि स मां द्वेष्टि यस्तमनु स मामनु ।\nइति संकल्प्यतां बुद्ध्या शरीरार्धं ममार्जुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He who hates him hates me, and he who follows him follows me. Understand in your mind that Arjuna is half my body.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"यथा त्वमप्रभातायामस्यां निशि रथोत्तमम् ।\nकल्पयित्वा यथाशास्त्रमादाय व्रतसंयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So, before dawn in this night, prepare my best chariot as the scriptures prescribe, and be ready, firm in your vow.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"गदां कौमोदकीं दिव्यां शक्तिं चक्रं धनुः शरान् ।\nआरोप्य वै रथे सूत सर्वोपकरणानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Charioteer, put on the chariot the divine mace Kaumodaki, the dart, discus, bow, arrows and all the equipment.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"स्थानं हि कल्पयित्वा च रथोपस्थे ध्वजस्य मे ।\nवैनतेयस्य वीरस्य समरे रथशोभिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Make a place on the chariot-seat for my banner, with Garuda, the son of Vinata, a hero shining on a chariot in battle.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"छत्रं जाम्बूनदैर्जालैरर्कज्वलनसंनिभैः ।\nविश्वकर्मकृतैर्दिव्यैरश्वानपि च भूषितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Also my parasol with nets of Jambunada gold shining like the sun and fire, and the horses adorned with divine ornaments made by Vishvakarman.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"बलाहकं मेघपुष्पं सैन्यं सुग्रीवमेव च ।\nयुक्त्वा वाजिवरान्यत्तः कवची तिष्ठ दारुक ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Yoke the best horses Balahaka, Meghapushpa, Shaibya and Sugriva, and stand ready in armour, Daruka.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"पाञ्चजन्यस्य निर्घोषमार्षभेणैव पूरितम् ।\nश्रुत्वा तु भैरवं नादमुपयाया जवेन माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When you hear the terrible sound of the Panchajanya, filled by a bull-like breath, come to me swiftly.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"एकाह्नाहममर्षं च सर्वदुःखानि चैव ह ।\nभ्रातुः पितृष्वसेयस्य व्यपनेष्यामि दारुक ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In a single day, Daruka, I shall remove the anger and all the sorrows of my cousin, my father's sister's son.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"सर्वोपायैर्यतिष्यामि यथा बीभत्सुराहवे ।\nपश्यतां धार्तराष्ट्राणां हनिष्यति जयद्रथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I shall try by every means that Bibhatsu kills Jayadratha in battle in front of Dhritarashtra's sons.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"यस्य यस्य च बीभत्सुर्वधे यत्नं करिष्यति ।\nआशंसे सारथे तत्र भवितास्य ध्रुवो जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Charioteer, I expect that whomever Bibhatsu makes an effort to kill, victory over him will certainly be his.\""}},{"text":"दारुक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Daruka said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"जय एव ध्रुवस्तस्य कुत एव पराजयः ।\nयस्य त्वं पुरुषव्याघ्र सारथ्यमुपजग्मिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Victory is certain for him whose charioteer you are, tiger among men. How could there be defeat?\""}},{"n":41,"text":"एवं चैतत्करिष्यामि यथा मामनुशाससि ।\nसुप्रभातामिमां रात्रिं जयाय विजयस्य हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I shall do as you instruct me. May this night dawn well, for victory and success.\""}}]}]}